5. How to Win 3.1  - WARNING! MAJOR MONGO SPOILERS! NOT FOR THE FAINTHEARTED!
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ok, now then.  The typical nethacker will grab all of his list of major 
needed magic items and immediately head for the Wizard.  Teleport down 
levels, magic map back up and Yo!  There's the Wizard!  Ok... he zooms in on 
the Wizard, nukes the Wiz with his +50 Sledgehammer named Oblivion (not an 
acutal new artifact), and grabs the...  Wait a minute!  The Wizard of Yendor 
does NOT have the Amulet!  What on earth do you do?

Well, here's a step-by-step list of what to do to win.  First of all, you 
will need to have defeated three opponents.  The first is the Dark One, 
located in the Quest levels.  One of the items that he is carrying is a bell, 
which will identify as a Chime of Opening.  The second is Vlad the Impaler, 
who will be carrying a candelabra, which will identify as a Candelabra of 
Invocation.  The third is the Wizard of Yendor, who will be carrying a book 
which will identify as the Book of the Dead.  Somewhere along the line you 
will also need to pick up seven candles.  These can usually be purchased from 
the lighting shop which will be located on the Mine Town level.

Now then...  level teleport down to level 55.  That's the lowest level that 
you're normally able to teleport to.  You will undoubtedly have noticed 
already (if you've played much) that there is a sort of level teleport 
barrier at the Valley of the Dead, so if you're above the Valley of the Dead 
it will take two level teleports to get to level 55 (if you're above the 
Valley of the Dead and try to teleport to below it, the game drops you out of 
teleport at the Valley of the Dead).

You will need to explore level 55 until you find a spot that says "You feel a 
strange vibration under your feet."  There is only one (random) spot that 
says this, and there's no way I've been able to find out which is the right 
spot other than just wandering around the whole level (except playing in 
Wizard Mode). 

Now then, make sure that your candelabrum is loaded.  You can do this by 
activating the candles that you have.  It will ask you if you want to put 
them in the candelabrum - say yes.  Then light the candelabrum by activating 
it.  The candles will burn brightly.

Next, ring the Chime of Opening by activating it.

Finally, read the Book of the Dead.  In a pretty cool display of text 
graphics an area will erupt around your feet, surrounding you with a moat, 
and you will see a stairway going down.  This stairway leads to the Sanctum 
Level.  An example Sanctum Level is shown below: 

