You will show up at the down staircase.  This level is crawling with priests 
of Moloch, but the area you want to head for is the central temple that you 
can see off to the left.  In that temple you will find the High Priest of 
Moloch.  He's got the Amulet of Yendor (presumably entrusted to his 
safekeeping by the Wizard of Yendor after the Wiz got tired of hackers 
constantly ripping it off from him).  Note that you will also incur the wrath 
of Moloch when you attack his High Priest.  Oh well - life's a... uh, well... 
you fill in the rest. 

Once you've got the Amulet you've got to begin that long trek upwards, 
because yes, when the Amulet of Yendor is in your possession, no matter what 
you do you will be totally unable to level teleport (even in Wizard Mode - 
that stinks).  Fifty-six levels later, you'll be standing on that top 
staircase, ready to go up to the end level.  Go up the staircase, and when it 
tells you to "Beware, for there is no return," GO FOR IT!

You'll find yourself on the Elemental Plane of Earth, and you'll promptly be 
attacked by the Wizard of Yendor yet again.  Nuke him, and then get on to 
exploring.  You will go through all of the Elemental Planes, and on each 
level there will be one randomly located spot on which there is a magic 
portal which leads to the next level.  These endgames are a bear to go 
through, but endure and you'll make it through.

I don't have screenshots of these levels, because they're basically open 
levels with not much on them.  Some notes:  On the Elemental Plane of Earth 
you MUST either be able to teleport, dig, or pass through earth (perhaps 
polymorphed into a xorn).  On the Elemental Plane of Fire you MUST be fire 
resistant (big shock there, eh?).  On the Elemental Plane of Air there are no 
musts, but it is a big help to be able to polymorph into something that can 
fly.  Otherwise you'll try moving and it will say "You tumble in the air," or 
"Moving through the air isn't easy," and so on.  It takes three or four 
keypresses to move each space and is generally a pain in the butt.  In my 
beta-test version, the Elemental Plane of Water somehow got skipped, but 
presumably it would be good to be able to walk on water or polymorph into 
something that can swim.

Once you've been through all the Elemental levels, you'll get to the final 
level, the Astral Plane.  This is where the final part of the endgame is.  
There are three temples (one for each alignment - recognize this part?), and 
the place is crawling with priests, angels, and other heavenly type beings.  
Make your way to the appropriate temple, sacrifice the Amulet, and hey 
presto!  You've just ascended!  An example of the Astral Plane Level is shown 
